# Frontend environment.
#
# ONLY non-secret, public values belong here. Everything prefixed with VITE_ is
# compiled into the JavaScript bundle and readable by every visitor. Never put
# an API key, a JWT secret or a database URI in this file.

# Where the auth/API service lives, including the version prefix.
#
# Unset  -> the app selects the "not configured" adapter: the header, both
#           forms and all validation still render, and submitting says plainly
#           that accounts are not available yet. No fake session is issued.
# Set    -> the HTTP adapter takes over. No code change is needed.
#
# Local demo (see src/backend, `npm run dev:demo`):
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api/v1
#
# Deployed:
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.gurukul.app/api/v1
